    "summary": "Rain‑soaked Red Rocks ’82 delivers monster Let It Grow and a blazing Shakedown Street",
    "review": "July 28, 1982 at Red Rocks is one of those rain‑battered nights that turns into pure Dead magic. The band rides the storm with high‑octane energy from the opening “Shakedown Street” straight through a second set that’s packed with highlights – a soaring Althea, a monster Let It Grow, an incendiary Spanish Jam, and a heartfelt Black Peter that feels almost reverent against the thunder. Even with the rain pounding the tarps, the performances stay tight; Brent’s piano jangles over the mix, Phil finally cuts through on the jam, and Bill & Mickey lock in a “tree‑log” drum groove that fuels the improvisations. Jerry may be buried in one of the SBD mixes, but on the best recordings his tone is scorching, especially during Let It Grow and Shakedown Street, and his vocal delivery on “He’s Gone” and “Black Peter” adds an emotional punch. The night caps off with a sweet encore of “It’s All Over Now Baby Blue,” leaving the crowd buzzing long after the last note.",
